ut if I keep it, maybe I can form a pair later. \n\nBut with only one J2 left, it's a 50% chance. \n\nAlternatively, if I discard T8, which has two left, maybe someone takes it. \n\nI think the best move is to discard J2. Because it's a single and less likely to be needed. \n\nSo the answer is Play J2.\n", "output": "Evaluation: [Discarding J2 is the safest option as it's a single tile with only one remaining in the wall, reducing the chance of being claimed by others.]\nReason: [J2 has only one remaining in the unshown tiles, making it less likely to be needed by opponents for a pung. Keeping other tiles like T2 or B1/B2 might be more critical for forming chows or pairs.]\nAnswer: Play J2"}
